00:00:17,520 --> 00:00:21,490
我们正在赋予它们凭借自己学习进步的力量。
We're giving them the power to learn to move on their own.

6
00:00:23,900 --> 00:00:26,170
这些新的生命形式会变得
Will these new life-forms evolve

7
00:00:26,170 --> 00:00:29,100
比我们更聪明更能干吗？
to be smarter and more capable than us?

8
00:00:29,100 --> 00:00:32,540
还是我们会和机械融为一体？
Or will we choose to merge with the machines?

9
00:00:33,410 --> 00:00:36,640
机器人是人类进化的未来吗？
Are robots the future of human evolution?

10
00:00:38,040 --> 00:00:41,140
与摩根弗里曼穿越虫洞
Through The Wormhole

11
00:00:41,410 --> 00:00:46,090
空间、时间、生命本身,
Space,time,life itself.

12
00:00:48,320 --> 00:00:52,760
宇宙的奥秘，尽在穿越虫洞。
The secrets of the cosmos lie through the wormhole.

13
00:00:57,870 --> 00:01:01,870
机器人是人类进化的未来吗？

14
00:01:04,940 --> 00:01:07,370
我们人类喜欢认为自己
We humans like to think of ourselves

15
00:01:07,370 --> 00:01:09,740
处于进化的顶端。
as the pinnacle of evolution.

16
00:01:09,740 --> 00:01:14,480
我们确实是地球上最聪明的、最具适应力的生命形式。
We are the smartest,most adaptable form of life on earth.

17
00:01:14,480 --> 00:01:18,780
我们已经重塑这个世界来满足我们的需要。
We have reshaped the world to suit our needs.

18
00:01:18,790 --> 00:01:22,760
就像智人替代了直立猿人,
But just as homo sapiens replaced homo erectus,

19
00:01:22,760 --> 00:01:26,360
必然会有什么将会替代我们。
it's inevitable something will replace us.

20
00:01:26,360 --> 00:01:30,000
但假若我们能够自己制造继承人呢？
What if we're building our own successors?

21
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:34,670
就像我们学习走动、思考、感受自我一样,
Just as we learn to move,think,and feel for ourselves,

22
00:01:34,670 --> 00:01:38,570
我们现在正在给予机器人同样的能力。
we're now giving robots those same powers.

23
00:01:38,570 --> 00:01:40,570
这将会把我们带到什么样的境地？
Where will this lead?

24
00:01:40,570 --> 00:01:44,210
这是人类将会转变的形式吗？
Is this what humanity will become?

25
00:01:48,650 --> 00:01:53,890
少年时,我用一些备用部件造了一辆自行车。
When I was a teenager,I built a bicycle from spare parts.

26
00:01:53,890 --> 00:01:57,390
我造的自行车平衡性非常好,
My bicycle was so well-balanced,

27
00:01:57,390 --> 00:02:00,330
我可以推动它就保持平衡而不需要骑在上面。
I could jog alongside it without holding onto it.

28
00:02:02,360 --> 00:02:05,770
没人认为这怎么厉害,但却使我思考
Nobody was that impressed,but it made me think.

29
00:02:05,770 --> 00:02:08,200
我们有一天会拥有可以
Would we one day have machines

30
00:02:08,200 --> 00:02:12,510
完全凭借自身行动的机器吗？
that truly could move on their own?

31
00:02:12,510 --> 00:02:16,140
那个时候它们还会需要我们吗？
Would they even need us anymore?

32
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:26,770
剑桥大学的Daniel Wolpert
Daniel Wolpert of the university of Cambridge

33
00:02:26,770 --> 00:02:28,170
认为如果机器人
believes that if robots

34
00:02:28,170 --> 00:02:30,680
是人类进化的未来,
are to be the future of human evolution,

35
00:02:30,680 --> 00:02:35,750
它们就必须像我们一样学习行动...
they're going to have to learn to move as well as we do...

36
00:02:35,750 --> 00:02:39,580
因为行动是我们强大智慧的
Because movement is the supreme achievement

37
00:02:39,580 --> 00:02:40,890
最高成就。
of our powerful intellect.

38
00:02:40,890 --> 00:02:43,190
我认为我们能够提出的最基本的问题是,
The most fundamental question I think we can ever ask is,

39
00:02:43,190 --> 00:02:45,760
为什么以及何时动物进化出了脑？
why and when have animals ever evolved a brain?

40
00:02:45,760 --> 00:02:47,760
现在,当我问我的学生这个问题时,
Now,when I ask my students this question,

41
00:02:47,760 --> 00:02:48,260
他们会告诉我,
they'll tell me,

42
00:02:48,260 --> 00:02:50,730
我们用大脑来思考或感知世界,
we have ones to think or to perceive the world,

43
00:02:50,730 --> 00:02:52,030
但这是完全错误的。
and that's completely wrong.

44
00:02:52,230 --> 00:02:54,530
我们只因为一个原因而具有大脑,
We have a brain for one reason and one reason only,

45
00:02:54,530 --> 00:02:57,000
那就是要产生能够适应环境的复杂行为,
and that's to produce adaptable and complex movement,

46
00:02:57,000 --> 00:02:59,510
因为行为才是我们具有的
because movement is the only way we have

47
00:02:59,510 --> 00:03:01,410
唯一可以影响世界的方式。
of affecting the world around us.

48
00:03:01,410 --> 00:03:04,410
弗里曼: 我们大脑的各种智力
Freeman: All of our brains' intellectual capacity

