00:03:04,490 --> 00:03:06,390
都源于一个原始的动机--
grew from one primal motivation --

50
00:03:06,490 --> 00:03:09,960
学得如何更加擅长行动,
to learn how to move better.

51
00:03:09,960 --> 00:03:13,170
这包括我们用两条腿行走的能力,
It was our ability to walk on two legs,

52
00:03:13,170 --> 00:03:16,840
使用复杂的面部表情交谈和表露情感,
to speak and emote with complex facial movements,

53
00:03:16,840 --> 00:03:19,770
并灵巧的控制四肢
and to manipulate our dexterous limbs

54
00:03:19,770 --> 00:03:23,410
使人类站在食物链顶端。
that put humans on top of the food chain.

55
00:03:23,410 --> 00:03:24,850
如果没有行动的能力,
There can be no value

56
00:03:24,850 --> 00:03:27,410
感知、情感和思考
to perception or emotions or thinking

57
00:03:27,410 --> 00:03:29,120
都没有意义。
without the ability to act.

58
00:03:29,120 --> 00:03:30,650
所有的其他特征,
All those other features,

59
00:03:30,650 --> 00:03:34,020
比如记忆、认知、爱、恐惧都要发展为行为,
like memory,cognition,love,fear play into movement,

60
00:03:34,020 --> 00:03:35,960
这些都是大脑输出的最终结果。
which is the final output of the brain.

61
00:03:38,030 --> 00:03:40,330
弗里曼: 没有任何机器可以做出
Freeman: No machine could handle

62
00:03:40,330 --> 00:03:44,530
像我们每天做的多种复杂行为。
the huge variety of complex movements we perform every day.

63
00:03:46,870 --> 00:03:48,470
想象一个机器人
Just imagine a robot

64
00:03:48,470 --> 00:03:51,970
想要玩一场英格兰最流行的消遣游戏。
trying to play one of England's most famous pastimes.

65
00:03:57,180 --> 00:03:59,180
尽管这次击球看起来很简单,
So,although that shot looks simple

66
00:03:59,180 --> 00:04:00,750
对于我来说毫不费力,
and it felt effortless to me,

67
00:04:00,750 --> 00:04:02,420
而我脑中进行的则是非常复杂的
the complexity of what's going on in my brain

68
00:04:02,420 --> 00:04:03,620
肢体协调。
is really quite remarkable.

69
00:04:03,620 --> 00:04:06,020
我必须注意投球手投出的球,
I have to follow the ball as the bowler bowls it

70
00:04:06,020 --> 00:04:07,990
并预测它会弹到哪里,
and predict where it's going to bounce

71
00:04:07,990 --> 00:04:09,220
以及它如何从地面弹起。
and how it's gonna rise from the ground.

72
00:04:09,220 --> 00:04:10,520
然后我需要作出决定
I then have to make a decision

73
00:04:10,520 --> 00:04:12,390
我要如何去击球,
as to what type of shot I'm going to make.

74
00:04:12,390 --> 00:04:15,060
最终,我需要协调600块肌肉
And finally,I have to contract my 600 muscles

75
00:04:15,060 --> 00:04:17,700
通过特定的顺序来进行击球动作。
in a particular sequence to execute the shot.

76
00:04:17,700 --> 00:04:19,300
此时,每一块肌肉的运动
Now,each of those components

77
00:04:19,300 --> 00:04:21,270
都经过了复杂的数学运算,
has real mathematical complexity,

78
00:04:21,270 --> 00:04:24,670
而这种能力现今远超所有的机器人。
which is currently beyond the ability of any robotic device.

79
00:04:24,670 --> 00:04:27,240
弗里曼: 让机器人拥有
Freeman: One of the greatest challenges

80
00:04:27,240 --> 00:04:29,040
我们这样行为的最大挑战之一
in getting robots to move like we do

81
00:04:29,040 --> 00:04:33,180
就是要让它们学会处理不确定因素--
is teaching them to deal with uncertainty --

82
00:04:33,180 --> 00:04:36,880
而对于我们的大脑来说这是本能。
something our brains do intrinsically.

83
00:04:36,880 --> 00:04:40,020
球不会以两次相同的情况飞向你,
A ball will never come at you the same way twice.

84
00:04:42,390 --> 00:04:46,030
每次你都必须要迅速调整动作。
You must instantly adjust your swing each time.

85
00:04:49,030 --> 00:04:51,000
问题是...
The question is...

86
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:54,800
人脑如何处理这些不确定因素？
How does the human brain deal with all this uncertainty?

87
00:04:54,800 --> 00:04:59,070
Daniel认为这需要一种概率估计理论
Daniel thinks it uses a theory of probability estimation

88
00:04:59,070 --> 00:05:00,970
称作贝叶斯推理,
【贝叶斯推理是由英国牧师贝叶斯发现的一种归纳推理方法,
与经典的统计归纳推理方法相比,贝叶斯推理在得出结论时不仅要根据当前所观察到的样本信息,
而且还要根据推理者过去有关的经验和知识。】
called bayesian inference

89
00:05:00,970 --> 00:05:02,680
才能进行运算。
to figure it out.

90
00:05:02,680 --> 00:05:05,810
Wolpert: 击球手现在要做的很重要的事情
Wolpert: So,a critical thing the batsman now has to do

91
00:05:05,810 --> 00:05:08,080
就是这个球会在哪里弹起,
is decide where this ball is going to bounce,

92
00:05:08,080 --> 00:05:10,120
只要他们能够准确击球,
so as they can prepare the correct shot,

93
00:05:10,120 --> 00:05:12,290
就需要贝叶斯推理。
and for that,they need bayesian inference.

94
00:05:12,290 --> 00:05:14,350
贝叶斯推理可以做的是
What bayesian inference is all about

95
00:05:14,350 --> 00:05:17,290
从两种不同的信息来源中
is deciding,optimally,the bounce location of the ball

96
00:05:17,290 --> 00:05:19,790
决定球会弹起的最准确的位置。
from two different sources of information.

97
00:05:19,790 --> 00:05:22,260
弗里曼: 一个信息来源是很明显的,
Freeman: One source of information is obvious.

98
00:05:22,260 --> 00:05:26,070
就是你盯着球。
You look at the ball.

99
00:05:26,070 --> 00:05:28,740
Wolpert: 你可以通过观察球飞来的
Wolpert: So,you can use vision of the trajectory of the ball

100
00:05:28,740 --> 00:05:30,000
运动轨迹
as it comes in

101
00:05:30,000 --> 00:05:32,210
来尝试估计它会在哪里弹起。
to try and estimate where it's going to bounce.

102
00:05:32,210 --> 00:05:33,710
但是视觉并不完美,
But vision is not perfect,

103
00:05:33,710 --> 00:05:36,780
因为我们对视觉的加工存在变动,
in that we have variability in our visual processors,

104
00:05:36,780 --> 00:05:39,040
所以至少落地点的变动范围就是红色圆圈显示的,
so at least where distribution's shown in red here

105
00:05:39,050 --> 00:05:41,120
作为球会落在某一点的概率分布。
as the probable bounce locations.

106
00:05:41,120 --> 00:05:45,290
但贝叶斯规则说还有一个信息来源,
But bayes' rule says there's another source of information.

107
00:05:45,290 --> 00:05:48,490
就是关于落地点的先验知识。【先验知识 是先于经验的知识】
It's the prior knowledge about possible bounce locations.

108
00:05:48,490 --> 00:05:50,020
如果你是个好击球手,
If you're a good batter,

109
00:05:50,020 --> 00:05:52,290
你就能有效地看着投球手
then you can effectively look at the bowler

110
00:05:52,290 --> 00:05:56,560
就能通过他特殊的投球方式或暗示了解到球的运行方式--
and maybe know by his particular bowling style or small cues --

111
00:05:56,560 --> 00:05:58,460
这里用蓝色底纹表示--
and that's shown by the blue shading --

112
00:05:58,470 --> 00:05:59,670
这是一个不同的区域。
which is a different area.

113
00:05:59,670 --> 00:06:02,040
那么贝叶斯推理就整合了
So,bayesian inference is a way of combining

114
00:06:02,040 --> 00:06:04,610
红色范围和蓝色范围,
this red distribution with the blue distribution,

115
00:06:04,610 --> 00:06:07,640
你通过两种信息的交集
and you do that by multiplying the numbers together in each

116
00:06:07,640 --> 00:06:09,680
产生了这个黄色分布,
to generate this yellow distribution,

117
00:06:09,680 --> 00:06:11,480
这个分布称为可信度。
which is termed the belief.

118
00:06:11,480 --> 00:06:13,050
通过使用这样的信息,
And using that information,

119
00:06:13,050 --> 00:06:15,280
击球手现在就可以准备击球了。
the batsman can now prepare his shot.

120
00:06:15,280 --> 00:06:17,780
好吧,我应该躲开一点。
Okay,I should probably get out of the way.

121
00:06:20,090 --> 00:06:22,760
弗里曼: 击球手的大脑,就像我们所有人,
Freeman: The batsman's brain,like all of ours,

122
00:06:22,760 --> 00:06:26,030
自动进行了这些计算。
is doing this math automatically.

123
00:06:26,030 --> 00:06:29,460
我们这个物种锤炼出了对于行为的预测,
We are a species that's honed for movement prediction.

124
00:06:29,460 --> 00:06:31,300
这就使我们成为了
It's what has made us

125
00:06:31,300 --> 00:06:36,270
这颗星球上最好的猎人和工具匠。
the planet's best hunters and toolmakers.

126
00:06:36,270 --> 00:06:39,210
我们已经有了比我们行动
We already have robots that are faster and more accurate

127
00:06:39,210 --> 00:06:42,140
更快更准确的机器人。
than we are.

128
00:06:42,140 --> 00:06:45,210
但是我们要为它们的每个行为编程,
But we have to program their every move.

129
00:06:45,210 --> 00:06:48,850
机器人只能沿着我们已经走过的
For robots to walk down the evolutionary road

130
00:06:48,850 --> 00:06:50,720
进化道路前进,
we've already traveled,

131
00:06:50,720 --> 00:06:53,720
它们要自己学会行动。
they're going to have to learn to move on their own.

132
00:06:55,160 --> 00:06:57,160
然后会发生什么呢？
What happens then?

