The computer deletes the robots

167
00:08:44,880 --> 00:08:46,750
做的不好的机器人,
that aren't doing a very good job,

168
00:08:46,750 --> 00:08:48,650
并保留下了做的
and the computer then takes the robots

169
00:08:48,650 --> 00:08:50,490
稍微好一点的机器人,
that are doing a slightly better job

170
00:08:50,490 --> 00:08:53,020
对它们进行改进,
and makes modified copies of them

171
00:08:53,020 --> 00:08:55,990
一次次重复这个过程。
and repeats this process over and over again.

172
00:08:55,990 --> 00:09:01,030
这样过了一会儿,计算机开始发现一些
And after a while,the computer starts to discover robots

173
00:09:01,030 --> 00:09:03,100
在这个例子中,能够从屏幕的左侧
that,in this case,are able to walk

174
00:09:03,100 --> 00:09:06,540
行走到屏幕右侧的机器人。
from the left side of the screen to the right side of the screen.

175
00:09:08,770 --> 00:09:12,570
弗里曼: 这是一个加速的进化过程,
Freeman: This is evolution on steroids.

176
00:09:12,570 --> 00:09:16,550
大自然花去了数百万年的时间,
What took mother nature millions of years

177
00:09:16,550 --> 00:09:20,150
而在计算机中只进行了几个小时。
takes the computer just a few hours.

178
00:09:20,150 --> 00:09:23,750
经过一夜,计算机测试了上千代机器人,
Overnight,the computer tests thousands of generations,

179
00:09:23,750 --> 00:09:28,990
最终产生了一个达到目标的机器人。
and eventually it produces a robot that meets the goal.

180
00:09:28,990 --> 00:09:31,160
当这个模拟创造出了
When the simulation makes something

181
00:09:31,160 --> 00:09:33,360
看起来非常有趣的东西时,
that looks particularly interesting,

182
00:09:33,360 --> 00:09:37,060
Hod和Josh就采用这种形体方案并将其建造出来。
Hod and Josh take that body plan and build it.

183
00:09:37,070 --> 00:09:39,100
现在他们能够测试
Now they can test whether

184
00:09:39,100 --> 00:09:42,270
计算机模拟中成功的行走方案
the strategies for moving learned in simulation

185
00:09:42,270 --> 00:09:44,870
能否应用于现实世界中。
work as well in the real world.

186
00:09:44,870 --> 00:09:48,380
这个机器人叫做正方形四脚机器人,
So,this robot is called the quadratot,

187
00:09:48,380 --> 00:09:51,650
它基本上算是一个正在通过机器人进化技术
and it's basically a robot that learns how to walk

188
00:09:51,650 --> 00:09:53,450
学习如何行走的机器人。
using evolutionary robotic techniques.

189
00:09:53,850 --> 00:09:55,780
我们在这里看到的
And so,what we can see here

190
00:09:55,780 --> 00:09:59,190
就是这个机器人如何学习的例子。
is a particular example of how this robot learns.

191
00:09:59,190 --> 00:10:02,260
这是它做出的最开始的步伐,
This is one of the earliest gaits that it did,

192
00:10:02,260 --> 00:10:05,960
我们能发现它移动的不是很远很快。
and we can see that it's not moving very far or very fast.

193
00:10:05,960 --> 00:10:08,200
有点像小孩,
It's kind of like a child

194
00:10:08,200 --> 00:10:11,200
很小的时候只会爬的动作。
during its very early behaviors of crawling.

195
00:10:11,200 --> 00:10:13,140
它正在尝试不同的方法,
It's trying out different things.

196
00:10:13,140 --> 00:10:15,940
一些更有利行走的,或是不利于行走的。
Some things work better. Some things work less well.

197
00:10:15,940 --> 00:10:18,870
它正在获得经验,从中学习,
And it's taking the experiences and learning from them

198
00:10:18,870 --> 00:10:20,840
并逐渐改善自己的步伐。
and gradually improving its gait.

199
00:10:20,840 --> 00:10:24,280
弗里曼: 已经存在许多机器人可以通过
Freeman: There are many robots that can move well

200
00:10:24,280 --> 00:10:28,480
预先编写的特定程序完美运动,
while executing a specific predesigned task.

201
00:10:28,480 --> 00:10:32,120
但是Hod和Josh的机器人
But Hod and Josh's robots

202
00:10:32,120 --> 00:10:34,960
则需要在新环境中
must start to learn by themselves from scratch

203
00:10:34,960 --> 00:10:37,690
全靠自己开始学习。
in an unknown environment.

204
00:10:37,690 --> 00:10:39,960
它能够感觉到自己的进步,
It can sense its own progress,

205
00:10:39,960 --> 00:10:42,360
像婴儿从爬行开始学习一样,
and like a baby learning to crawl,

206
00:10:42,360 --> 00:10:44,270
通过每走一步以及每次跌倒,
it becomes more aware of its body

207
00:10:44,470 --> 00:10:45,800
它越来越能意识到自己的身体。
with every step and every tumble.

208
00:10:46,000 --> 00:10:48,970
Hod和Josh认为这种自我认知
Hod and Josh believe this self-awareness

209
00:10:48,970 --> 00:10:54,470
逐渐会构成意识的基础形式。
gradually builds into a basic form of consciousness.

210
00:10:54,470 --> 00:10:56,570
通常我们都会问到,
Often,we've raised the question,

211
00:10:56,570 --> 00:10:58,880
什么是有意识的,什么没有？
is something conscious,or is it not?

212
00:10:58,880 --> 00:11:00,540
但它的确不是一个黑白分明的东西,
But it's really not a black-and-white thing.

213
00:11:00,540 --> 00:11:01,780
它更像是关于
It's more about

214
00:11:01,780 --> 00:11:05,410
一个实体能多大程度具有自我这一概念,
to what degree an entity's able to conceive of itself,

215
00:11:05,420 --> 00:11:08,090
多大程度的模拟自己、考虑自己 、
to simulate itself,to think about itself,

216
00:11:08,090 --> 00:11:09,820
具有自我意识。
to be self-aware.

217
00:11:09,820 --> 00:11:13,760
就像机器人通过多种复杂方式学习移动,
As robots learn to move in more complex ways,

218
00:11:13,760 --> 00:11:17,190
它们就有可能发展出和我们同等的意识,
it's possible they will develop levels of consciousness

219
00:11:17,190 --> 00:11:20,460
甚至超越于我们的意识。
equal to ours and maybe beyond.

220
00:11:21,830 --> 00:11:23,900
不过根据一位科学家的说法,
But according to one scientist,

221
00:11:23,900 --> 00:11:26,870
一个机器人若真的拥有意识...
for a robot to become truly conscious...

222
00:11:28,310 --> 00:11:31,210
...它就必须具有情感。
...it must develop feelings.

223
00:11:33,000 --> 00:11:35,330
意识是什么？
What is consciousness?

224
00:11:35,830 --> 00:11:39,870
这要看你问谁了,
The answer depends on who you talk to.

225
00:11:39,870 --> 00:11:43,770
一位医生对意识的定义可能会不同于牧师,
A doctor's definition would be different from a priest's.

226
00:11:43,770 --> 00:11:47,110
但我们都认为我们的高层次意识
But we all agree that our high-level consciousness

227
00:11:47,110 --> 00:11:49,950
将我们与其他生物体区分开,
is what separates us from other organisms

228
00:11:49,950 --> 00:11:52,980
当然也与机器人区分开。
and,of course,from robots.

229
00:11:52,980 --> 00:11:57,520
要用什么办法才能让机器人拥有意识呢？
What would it take for robots to become conscious?

230
00:11:57,520 --> 00:12:01,860
它们能通过单纯的逻辑发展出意识吗？
Can they get there on logic alone?

231
00:12:01,860 --> 00:12:05,560
还是必须要学会感受？
Or must they also learn to feel?

232
00:12:07,730 --> 00:12:12,300
来自伊利诺伊大学的Pentti Haikonen教授认为
Professor Pentti Haikonen from the university of Illinois

233
00:12:12,300 --> 00:12:15,810
机器人只能在它们可以体验感情后
believes machines will only become conscious

234
00:12:15,810 --> 00:12:18,670
才能发展出意识。
when they can experience emotions.

235
00:12:18,670 --> 00:12:22,240
他从很小的时候开始就有着这种观点,
It's a belief he has held since he was very young

236
00:12:22,240 --> 00:12:26,280
也是他第一次思考意识的意义时。
when he first contemplated what it meant to be conscious.

237
00:12:26,280 --> 00:12:31,490
还是4、5岁的样子,我站在家里的厨房中,
When I was 4 or 5 years old,I was standing in our kitchen,

238
00:12:31,490 --> 00:12:36,490
突然被一种神秘的存在感惊呆了...
and suddenly I was struck by the mystery of existence...

239
00:12:37,890 --> 00:12:41,400
...为什么我会是我,
...how and why I was me

240
00:12:41,400 --> 00:12:45,940
而不是我姐姐或哥哥,
and why I was not my sister or my brother.

241
00:12:45,940 --> 00:12:49,840
我是如何进到我的身体中的？
How did I get inside myself?

242
00:12:51,070 --> 00:12:53,110
弗里曼: 随着他的长大,
Freeman: As he got older,

243
00:12:53,110 --> 00:12:57,250
Pentti意识到使他感受到意识的
Pentti realized that what made him feel conscious

244
00:12:57,250 --> 00:12:58,980
就是他脑中
of being inside his head

245
00:12:58,980 --> 00:13:01,680
对于身边世界中人和物的
were his emotional reactions to the people and objects

246
00:13:01,680 --> 00:13:03,750
各种情绪反应。
in the world around him.

247
00:13:05,590 --> 00:13:09,090
我们意识背后的神经活动
The neural processes that are behind our consciousness

248
00:13:09,090 --> 00:13:11,990
发生于我们的脑内,
take place inside our brain,

249
00:13:11,990 --> 00:13:14,300
但是我们并不以这种方式看世界。
but we don't see things that way.

250
00:13:14,300 --> 00:13:16,900
举个例子,当你扎破你的手指时,
For instance,when you cut your finger,

251
00:13:16,900 --> 00:13:20,770
手指的疼痛感就这么出现了,
the pain is in the finger or so it appears,

252
00:13:20,770 --> 00:13:24,040
但实际上疼痛感在这里。
but,actually,the pain is in here.

253
00:13:24,040 --> 00:13:27,240
有了感受才意味着意识。
To feel is to be conscious.

254
00:13:29,810 --> 00:13:33,850
弗里曼: 我们的大脑对于周围世界的
Freeman: Our brain's raw experience of the world around us

255
00:13:33,850 --> 00:13:36,550
原始感受只是通过我们的感觉产生的
is just a series of electrical impulses

256
00:13:36,550 --> 00:13:39,560
一系列的电脉冲,
generated by our senses.

257
00:13:39,560 --> 00:13:44,330
只是我们把这些电脉冲与相关的情感
However,we translate these impulses into mental images

258
00:13:44,330 --> 00:13:48,200
转译成了心理表象。
by making emotional associations with them.

259
00:13:50,000 --> 00:13:52,570
令人愉悦的声音,
A sound is pleasing.

260
00:13:52,570 --> 00:13:54,900
平静安详的景象。
A view is peaceful.

261
00:13:54,900 --> 00:13:57,940
根据Pentti的理解,意识只是
Consciousness,according to Pentti,

262
00:13:57,940 --> 00:14:02,610
承载着多种心理表象的马赛克。
is just a rich mosaic of emotionally laden mental images.

263
00:14:02,610 --> 00:14:06,880
他认为要使得一个机器人真正具有意识,
He believes that to have a truly conscious machine,

264
00:14:06,880 --> 00:14:09,250
你就必须赋予它们
you must give it the power

265
00:14:09,250 --> 00:14:13,020
将感官数据与情绪联系起来的能力。
to associate sensory data with emotions.

266
00:14:13,020 --> 00:14:17,590
而这个机器人,它已经具有了这种能力。
And in this robot,he has begun that process.

267
00:14:17,590 --> 00:14:19,960
这是第一个机器人
This is the first robot

268
00:14:19,960 --> 00:14:23,500
可以使用这种神经网络联系,
that utilizes associative neural networks.

269
00:14:23,500 --> 00:14:26,770
这和我们人类的学习方式有些类似。
It is the same kind of learning that we humans use.

270
00:14:26,770 --> 00:14:28,740
当我们看到或听到一些东西时,
When we see and hear something,

271
00:14:28,740 --> 00:14:31,540
我们会把这两种感觉联系起来,
we make a connection between those things,

272
00:14:31,540 --> 00:14:35,380
之后的日子中如果我们看到或者听到同样的事情,
and later on when we see or hear the other thing,

273
00:14:35,380 --> 00:14:38,250
我们就会感受到相对应的另一种感觉。
the other thing comes to our mind.

274
00:14:38,250 --> 00:14:42,620
弗里曼: xrc-1机器人像我们一样
Freeman: The xcr-1 experiences the world

275
00:14:42,620 --> 00:14:45,450
直接感受这个世界。
directly through its senses like we do.

276
00:14:45,450 --> 00:14:50,330
它有一些基本的触觉、视觉和听觉。
On board are the basics of touch,sight,and sound.

277
00:14:51,790 --> 00:14:56,100
Pentti已经开始赋予其情感
Pentti has begun the process of giving it emotional associations

278
00:14:56,100 --> 00:14:58,600
与特定感知数据的联系,
to specific sensory data,

279
00:14:58,600 --> 00:15:00,870
比如绿色。
like the color green.

280
00:15:00,870 --> 00:15:04,240
Pentti在这个机器人前面放置一个绿色物体,
Pentti places a green object in front of the robot,

281
00:15:04,240 --> 00:15:05,640
它能够识别。
which it recognizes.

282
00:15:05,640 --> 00:15:07,280
绿色。
Green.

283
00:15:07,280 --> 00:15:10,550
然后他给它一个不好的联系--
Then he gives green a bad association --

284
00:15:10,550 --> 00:15:13,580
从后侧猛击它。
a smack on the backside.

285
00:15:13,580 --> 00:15:18,890
这种对于联系的学习就像小孩子一样。
The associative learning is similar to little children.

286
00:15:18,890 --> 00:15:20,060
疼。
Hurt.

287
00:15:20,060 --> 00:15:24,690
你可以告诉孩子这个不好或这是好的,
And you say that this is not good or this is good,

288
00:15:24,690 --> 00:15:28,960
或者揍孩子。
or you may also smack the little child.

289
00:15:28,960 --> 00:15:30,570
疼。
Hurt.

290
00:15:30,570 --> 00:15:32,070
当然我并不建议这么做。
I don't recommend that.

291
00:15:33,300 --> 00:15:35,900
绿色,不好。
Green bad.

292
00:15:35,900 --> 00:15:38,310
机器人对于绿色物体的心理意象
Freeman: The robot's mental image of the green object

293
00:15:38,310 --> 00:15:42,240
现在联系上了不好的情绪。
is now associated with the emotion bad.

294
00:15:42,240 --> 00:15:46,950
从现在开始,它会一直避着绿色瓶子。
And from now on,it will avoid the green bottle.

295
00:15:46,950 --> 00:15:50,320
但这并不是xrc-1所有的学习部分,
But it's not all pain for the xcr-1.

296
00:15:50,320 --> 00:15:52,290
就像我们教机器人
Just like we teach the robot

297
00:15:52,290 --> 00:15:55,220
把疼痛联系上了绿色物体,
to associate pain with the green object,

298
00:15:55,220 --> 00:15:57,130
我们也能够教机器人
we can teach the robot

299
00:15:57,130 --> 00:16:00,160
把愉快和其他物体联系起来,
to associate,also,pleasure with objects,

300
00:16:00,160 --> 00:16:04,500
这个例子中是一个蓝色物体。
in this case with the blue object,like this.

301
00:16:04,500 --> 00:16:05,500
蓝色。
Blue.

302
00:16:05,500 --> 00:16:07,540
弗里曼: 为了让它把蓝色联系上好的感觉,
Freeman: To give blue a good association,

303
00:16:07,540 --> 00:16:11,540
Pentti轻轻抚摸机器人顶部。
Pentti gently strokes the top of the robot.

304
00:16:11,540 --> 00:16:14,180
蓝色,好。
Blue good.

305
00:16:15,000 --> 00:16:18,230
这个简单的实验证明了
This simple experiment demonstrates

306
00:16:18,230 --> 00:16:24,370
这个机器人具有对物体的心理意象
that this robot has mental images of objects

307
00:16:24,370 --> 00:16:26,670
和心理内容。
and mental content.

308
00:16:26,670 --> 00:16:29,180
弗里曼: 这还是它发展成长的早期,
Freeman: It's still early in its development,

309
00:16:29,180 --> 00:16:33,380
但xcr-1已经学会了基本的情绪反应,
but the xcr-1 has learned the basics of emotional reaction

310
00:16:33,380 --> 00:16:35,980
从害怕...
from fear...

311
00:16:35,980 --> 00:16:38,320
绿色,不好。
Green bad.

312
00:16:44,690 --> 00:16:47,400
绿色,不好。
Green bad.

313
00:16:50,860 --> 00:16:52,200
到渴望。
...to desire.

314
00:16:52,200 --> 00:16:55,030
蓝色,好。
Blue good.

315
00:16:55,040 --> 00:16:59,640
♪ Now's my time for love ♪

316
00:16:59,640 --> 00:17:02,510
♪ lonely moments seem to... ♪

317
00:17:02,510 --> 00:17:05,850
随着xrc-1更高级的版本中
As a more advanced version of the xcr-1

318
00:17:05,850 --> 00:17:07,820
存储着心理意象的记忆...
fills its memory with mental images...

319
00:17:07,820 --> 00:17:09,320
牙医,不好。
Dentist bad.

320
00:17:09,320 --> 00:17:11,090
...它就开始能够
...it will start to be able

321
00:17:11,090 --> 00:17:13,620
凭借自己与新环境互动,
to react to new situations on its own

322
00:17:13,620 --> 00:17:16,690
最终会像所有具有情绪波动的生物一样
and eventually experience the world

323
00:17:16,690 --> 00:17:20,060
体验这个世界。
much like any emotionally-driven being.

324
00:17:20,060 --> 00:17:22,030
我最大的梦想就是
It is my great dream

325
00:17:22,030 --> 00:17:25,870
我建造的机器人有一天能问
to build robot that is one day able to ask,

326
00:17:25,870 --> 00:17:29,970
“我是如何成为自己的呢？”
"How did I get inside myself?"

327
00:17:29,970 --> 00:17:33,110
弗里曼: 当机器人到达这种程度时,
Freeman: Once robots reach this point,

328
00:17:33,110 --> 00:17:35,980
什么还能阻止它们进步,
what's to stop them from moving on

329
00:17:35,980 --> 00:17:39,410
变成与我们不同的却有意识的东西？
and becoming conscious of things we're not?

330
00:17:39,410 --> 00:17:43,750
这个人认为机器人是人类的未来,
This man thinks robots will become the future of humanity

331
00:17:43,750 --> 00:17:47,290
因为它们具有我们缺乏的东西。
because they'll have something we lack.

332
00:17:47,290 --> 00:17:51,630
在最后一个说出"Eureka"的人类之后
Their brains will have the capacity for genius

333
00:17:51,630 --> 00:17:56,230
它们仍然会表现得非常天才。
long after the last human ever says "Eureka."

334
00:17:57,000 --> 00:18:00,930
阿基米德第一次在浴缸中喊出了Eureka,（因为发现浮力原理）
for Archimedes,Eureka happened in the bathtub.

335
00:18:00,930 --> 00:18:05,940
爱因斯坦在乘坐电车时想到了相对论,
Einstein was riding a streetcar when relativity dawned on him.

336
00:18:05,940 --> 00:18:09,980
这些杰出的思维都曾闪现出灵感,
These brilliant minds had a flash of inspiration

337
00:18:09,980 --> 00:18:12,940
推动了全人类的进步。
and drove all of humanity forward.

338
00:18:12,940 --> 00:18:16,180
但是今天的科学问题,
But the scientific questions of today,

339
00:18:16,180 --> 00:18:19,620
比如探索亚原子粒子的真相,
probing shoals of subatomic particles

